- README.SUSE, 90-sheepshaver.conf: SheepShaver-jit also needs the
  SELinux boolean mmap_low_allowed on Leap 16

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov  8 17:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Ship two binaries: SheepShaver (MEM_BULK, no JIT; runs out of the
  box) and SheepShaver-jit (real addressing + JIT; needs
  vm.mmap_min_addr=0). The precompiled x86_64 JIT ops assume real
  addressing and crash at boot with MEM_BULK or direct addressing
- Add README.SUSE and an example 90-sheepshaver.conf (docs only, not
  installed to /etc/sysctl.d); add a JIT action to the .desktop file
- ExclusiveArch: x86_64

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov  8 17:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Use -DMEM_BULK (as the Windows port does) instead of direct
  addressing, which crashed at boot with a New World ROM (Mac OS 8.6)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov  8 17:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Build with --enable-addressing=direct: the default real addressing
  maps page zero and fails with "Cannot map Low Memory Globals"
  unless vm.mmap_min_addr is 0

